              "text": "prōveniō, prōvenīre — \"to come forth, to grow; to turn out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Frūmentum hōc annō bene prōvēnit. The grain grew well this year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "prōveniō, prōvenīre, prōvēnī, prōventum. Of a harvest, to come up; of a plan, to turn out. English provenance comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
