          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "prōveniō is built from prō \"forth\" and veniō \"to come\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English provenance comes from it through French."
