              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "succēdō, succēdere — \"to turn out well, to succeed; to come next\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cōnsilium nōn successit. The plan did not succeed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "succēdō, succēdere, successī, successum. With the dative it is also to take someone's place. English succeed and success."
            }
          ]
        },
