          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "succēdō is built from sub \"up to, next\" and cēdō \"to go\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to come up close, to come next. English succeed and success come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
